## Development

```bash
uv run pytest                          # unit tests (tests/unit)
RUN_INTEGRATION=1 uv run pytest tests/integration   # integration tests (real services)
uv run ruff format .                   # format
uv run ruff check --fix .              # lint
uv run pre-commit run --all-files      # secrets, SAST, workflow lint/audit
```

Pull request titles must follow
[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/); they
drive versioning and the changelog. See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).

Coding agents follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). Claude Code also uses the shared
settings in `.claude/settings.json`: it can't read `.env` or credential files,
and asks before committing, pushing, or opening a PR (see "Claude Code" in
CONTRIBUTING.md).

## First push

One-time GitHub setup after creating the repository:

```bash
git add -A && git commit -m "chore: initial commit from python-template"
gh repo create [[ github_owner ]]/[[ project_name ]] --private --source . --push
```

Then, in the repository settings:

1. **Settings > General > Pull Requests**: allow squash merging only, and use
   the pull request title as the default commit message.
2. **Settings > Actions > General**: enable "Allow GitHub Actions to create and
   approve pull requests" so release-please can open its release PR (or set up
   the GitHub App described at the top of `.github/workflows/release.yml`).
3. **Settings > Branches** (optional): protect `main` and require the **CI**
   status check.

## Template updates

This project was generated from a [Copier](https://copier.readthedocs.io/)
template. Its location and version are recorded in `.copier-answers.yml`
(`_src_path` and `_commit`), which is where `copier update` pulls from. To pull
in later template improvements:

```bash
uvx copier update --trust
```

Copier merges the template's changes with yours and marks any conflicts. Your
answers are stored in `.copier-answers.yml`; don't edit it by hand. The one
exception: if the template moves to a new repository (one that doesn't
redirect from the old address), update `_src_path` there.
